    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Hunters Estate Agent are truly delighted to present No.5 The Birches, a home of distinction, positioned in a quiet, cul de sac setting. Nestled behind electric gates within a leisurely stroll of the village, this very fine Tudor-style five-bedroom detached residence is presented in excellent order and tastefully appointed throughout. \r\n\r\nA sweeping gravel drive provides an abundance of off-street parking, setting the tone for a property of real quality. Rooms of generous proportions extend to 372sq.m / 4,004sq.ft (excludes all garages & converted attic space) with a mahogany double door opening to a spacious reception hall featuring decorative ceiling coving and a centre rose. The principal reception rooms are of exceptional scale, including a drawing room centred around a majestic marble fireplace, a dining room and family room both finished with decorative coving and feature fireplaces, and a magnificent dual-aspect conservatory with vaulted ceiling and double doors opening onto the patio and gardens. The bespoke Andrew Ryan designed kitchen incorporates granite worktops, a feature island unit and quality Siemens appliances, while a well-appointed utility room and integral garage complete the ground floor.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, a striking main suite comprising bedroom, dressing room and ensuite is joined by four further well-proportioned bedrooms, one with its own ensuite, together with a beautifully appointed family bathroom incorporating a sunken bath. \r\n\r\nHand-crafted wardrobes designed by Irish Conservatories complete a specification of real distinction, while an integral garage provides generous storage, with scope for conversion should a new owner wish to extend the living accommodation further.  \r\n\r\nThe delightful, private rear gardens enjoy rolling lawns and a vast patio area, and are richly stocked with specimen trees, shrubs and herbaceous borders. The gardens benefit from a south facing all day sunny orientation.\r\n\r\nIdeally located just a short stroll from the charming Foxrock village, residents enjoy easy access to boutique shops, eateries, and premier sporting facilities including Foxrock Golf Club, Leopardstown Racecourse, and Carrickmines Lawn Tennis Club. The area is well served by renowned schools and excellent transport links via the N11 (QBC), M50, and LUAS.\r\n\r\nViewing is highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "ENTRANCE PORCH\r\n1.30m x 2.61m (4'3\" x 8'6\")\r\nApproached via a mahogany double door. Polished porcelain tiled floor. Double doors to: -\r\n\r\nRECEPTION HALL\r\n7.15m x 4.06m (23'5\" x 13'3\")\r\nDecorative ceiling coving, centre rose and radiator covers. Understairs storage and cloaks cupboard. Decorative wall lights and polished porcelain tiled floor.\r\n\r\nCLOAKS CUPBOARD\r\nFloor to ceiling wardrobes. Opening into: -\r\n\r\nGUEST WC\r\nWhite Armitage shanks suite incorporating a wash hand basin in vanity unit, wall mirror, heated towel rail and wc. Porcelain tiled walls and floor and recessed lighting.\r\n\r\nDRAWING ROOM\r\n6.89m x 5.67m (22'7\" x 18'7\")\r\nMajestic fireplace with marble inset and hearth. Decorative ceiling coving, centre rose and radiator covers.\r\n\r\nDINING ROOM\r\n4.8m x 3.5m (15'8\" x 11'5\")\r\nDecorative ceiling coving, centre rose and radiator covers.\r\n\r\nFAMILY ROOM\r\n5.78m x 4.23m (18'11\" x 13'10\")\r\nFeature marble fireplace flanked by library and entertainment units with lighting detail. Decorative ceiling coving and radiator cover. Double doors to: -\r\n\r\nCONSERVATORY\r\n13.46m x 4.44m (44'1\" x 14'6\")\r\nVaulted ceiling with recessed lighting detail. Decorative radiator covers and porcelain tiled floor. Dual aspect room with double doors to the patio and gardens.\r\n\r\nKITCHEN\r\n5m x 4.7m (16'4\" x 15'5\")\r\nBespoke Andrew Ryan designed kitchen incorporating granite worktop areas and granite surround and a Franke stainless steel sink and drainer. Quality Siemens appliances to include a built-in double oven, an induction hob and microwave, and an integrated dishwasher and an integrated Liebherr fridge freezer. Feature island unit with granite worktop ideal for casual dining. Decorative lighting and porcelain tiled floor.\r\n\r\nINTEGRAL GARAGE LEADS TO THE:\r\n\r\nUTILITY ROOM\r\n4.8m x 2.9m (15'8\" x 9'6\")\r\nFitted units with stainless steel sink and built-in Bosch washing machine and Zanussi dyer.\r\n\r\nSTAIRCASE TO FIRST FLOOR\r\n\r\nLANDING\r\n5.16m x 2.27m (16'11\" x 7'5\")\r\nDecorative ceiling coving. Hot press with insulated cylinder, dual immersion and timer. Access via a Stira Stairs to a converted attic with a large Velux window, providing a wonderful storage space.\r\n\r\nMAIN SUITE\r\n6.66m x 8.66m (21'10\" x 28'4\")\r\n\r\nBEDROOM\r\nFloor to ceiling fitted wardrobes.\r\n\r\nENSUITE\r\nWhite Armitage Shanks suite incorporating a shower with rain head and handheld spray, wash hand basin in vanity unit, wall mirror, heated towel rail and wc. Tiled walls and floor, recessed lighting.\r\n\r\nDRESSING ROOM\r\nFloor to ceiling shelving and hanging space.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nBEDROOM 2\r\n4.44m x 3.8m (14'6\" x 12'5\")\r\nFloor to ceiling fitted wardrobes.\r\n\r\nENSUITE\r\nWhite Althea suite incorporating a wash hand basin in vanity unit, power shower, wall mirror and wc. Under floor heating, tiled walls and recessed lighting.\r\n\r\nBATHROOM\r\n3m x 2.4m (9'10\" x 7'10\")\r\nWhite Armitage Shanks Suite incorporating a sunken bath, a shower unit, wash hand basin in vanity unit with marble surround, wall mirror, heated towel rail and wc. Tiled walls and floor and recessed lighting.\r\n\r\nBEDROOM 3\r\n4.44m x 4m (14'6\" x 13'1\")\r\nFloor to ceiling fitted wardrobes.\r\n\r\nBEDROOM 4\r\n4m x 3.76m (13'1\" x 12'4\")\r\nFloor to ceiling fitted wardrobes.\r\n\r\nBEDROOM 5\r\n3.33m x 2.53m (10'11\" x 8'3\")\r\nDecorative ceiling coving.\r\n\r\nSTIRA TO THE ATTIC\r\n6.8m x 4m (22'3\" x 13'1\")\r\nAn immense space with an abundance of light.\r\n\r\nOUTSIDE\r\nThe front of the property is approached via electric gates leading to a sweeping gravel driveway bordered by a lawn area and mature trees. The gated side passage leads to delightful, private south facing rear gardens enjoying rolling lawns and a vast patio area, and richly stocked with specimen trees, shrubs and herbaceous borders."
      },
